## Documentation

### Code Comments
- Explain WHY, not WHAT
- Document complex algorithms
- Note LinkedIn-specific quirks
- Include examples for non-obvious code

### README Updates
- Keep quick start guide current
- Document new flags/options
- Update troubleshooting section
- Include example outputs

## Performance Considerations

### Memory
- Clean up ElementHandles after use
- Don't store large objects in memory
- Stream data to CSV incrementally

### Speed
- Run independent operations in parallel
- Cache selectors when possible
- Minimize page interactions
- Use efficient DOM queries

## Security

### Credentials
- Never commit credentials
- Use environment variables
- Don't log sensitive data
- Sanitize URLs in logs

### Data Privacy
- Only scrape publicly available data
- Respect LinkedIn's terms of service
- Don't store unnecessary personal data
- Provide data deletion mechanisms

## Maintenance

### Regular Tasks
- Update dependencies monthly
- Test against LinkedIn changes
- Review and update selectors
- Clean up old logs and outputs

### When LinkedIn Changes
1. Identify what changed (DOM structure, selectors, etc.)
2. Update affected extractors
3. Test thoroughly
4. Document the change
5. Update selector fallbacks

